{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4f4680899a08649b","name":"RA-7 Protocol Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-4f4680899a08649b","title":"RA-7 Protocol Droid","revision":19552,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:10:45Z","sha256":"8c37fe8ac4e4bc6b99e821d0660e694d2fa2bc8eb9911909e77eb81d7b686d5b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19552","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=RA-7%20Protocol%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4f4680899a08649b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The RA-7 series of Protocol Droids is clearly an attempt by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arakyd Industries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arakyd_Industries","referenceId":"reference:53475569f2ae9d67"}," to duplicate most of the abilities of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["3PO-Series Protocol Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3PO-Series_Protocol_Droid","referenceId":"reference:0cbde42806fd4d2c"},", and in most respects it fails. The Droid is very similar in appearance to the 3PO, except for its bug-eyed head and stiffer gait. It is not as able as a 3PO unit, however, and in an effort to avoid the overly delicate personality of ",{"tag":"a","children":["3PO-Series Protocol Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3PO-Series_Protocol_Droids"},", the RA-7 was programmed to be \"stern.\" In truth, the personalities of these Droids tend to fall somewhere between taciturn and vindictive. Almost no one would willingly buy an RA-7 as an assistant- which is why the ISB gives them away as gifts.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In fact, the RA-7 is a plot by the ISB to keep tabs on everyone of questionable loyalty throughout the Empire. Though their numbers are only now starting to be large enough to be of real value, RA-7s are programmed to report on their owner's subversive or questionable activities by way of secret, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Internal Comlinks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Internal_Comlinks"},". Most RA-7s also have recording devices hidden within them, allowing them to gather hard evidence of their masters' failings and crimes. (The recorders are concealed, requiring a DC 30 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check to find.) The ISB hands them out mostly to mid-level officers and officials, generally right after a promotion. Many recipients see these gifts as a sign of rising station and influence, but a few have begun to realize that the ISB does nothing without a secondary purpose. Many officers \"lose\" their RA-7 Droids in short order, or send them into dangerous situations from which they never return.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["RA-7 Protocol Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["RA-7 Protocol Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.